  "operating_rule": "Family-agnostic shared infrastructure is admitted only through platform/certification/* branches. Stateful route-registry consumers are the machine-inventoried direct certification_routes surface plus existing shared successor-compatibility controls. Generic route-state semantic repairs belong on the platform lane; bounded family-transition registration/compatibility updates may remain on a family branch. Historical consumers must bind exact protected predecessor state, current-state consumers validate the live registry, transition consumers compare explicitly governed endpoints, and invariant consumers may inspect route-independent structure only. Canonical certification runs the invariant/shared core plus only the one unambiguously affected result-family control set; platform, non-pull-request, unknown, route-only without family evidence, and multi-family changes fail closed to the full validation estate. Family branches consume protected platform-only helpers and must not carry private revisions of them."
